# Files/dirs that should never end up in a Docker build context.
# Smaller context = faster builds + smaller chance of leaking secrets.

# --- VCS ---
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.gitattributes
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# --- Editor / OS noise ---
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
*.swo
Thumbs.db

# --- Local Python (we install fresh inside the image) ---
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/*.egg
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.local
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov

# --- Secrets / local config (NEVER bake into an image) ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.docker
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# --- Local databases ---
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.db-journal
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm

# --- Frontend tree: included for builds, but each subproject's own
#     .dockerignore trims node_modules / .next / secrets at copy time.
#     We exclude frontend/docs (none today, but keep it explicit),
#     frontend/.env files, and the AI-tool directories that should
#     never end up in an image. The frontend/ subdirectory itself is
#     NOT excluded — compose.yaml builds the frontend image. ---
docs
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
architecture.md
skills-lock.json
.impeccable
.agents
.claude
.codex
.cursor
.puku-cli

# --- Tests / eval (not needed at runtime) ---
**/tests
**/test_*.py
**/*_test.py
**/eval
**/requirements-eval.txt
.pytest_cache

# --- Docker / compose meta (don't recurse into itself) ---
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
compose.yaml
compose.*.yaml
compose.*.yml
DOCKER.md

# --- Logs / build artifacts ---
**/*.log
**/build
**/dist
**/.next
**/node_modules
**/.npm
**/.cache
**/.parcel-cache
**/.turbo
**/.eslintcache
